 DevOps Interview Command Series — Linux (Day 1) 🐧

Linux is the foundation of DevOps.
From CI/CD runners to containers, Kubernetes nodes, and cloud VMs — everything runs on Linux.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Linux commands you must know:

“ls -lAh | cd /path | pwd
cp -r src dst | mv old new | rm -rf file
chmod 755 file | chmod u+x script.sh | chown user:group file

ps -ef | grep process
top / htop
free -m | df -h | du -sh *
uptime

ip a
ss -tulnp
ping host
curl URL

cat file | less file
head -n 10 file
tail -f app.log
grep -i error app.log
awk '{print $1}'
sed 's/old/new/g'

systemctl status service
systemctl restart service
systemctl enable service
journalctl -u service

tar -cvf file.tar dir/
tar -xvf file.tar
gzip file

export VAR=value
env
history
alias ll='ls -l'”

🎯 Interview Focus
• Debug CPU & memory issues
• Identify processes using ports
• Analyze production logs
• Fix service & permission failures
